  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1833b97b4e8284e489c3555d5dace838, type: 3}
  m_Name: PY_02_DATA_TYPES
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: PY_02_DATA_TYPES
  language: 1
  topic: Data Types
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 2
  questionText: Fill in a value so b holds the text 42 (a string, not a number).
    The program then adds "!" to it.
  code: 'b = ____

    print(b + "!")'
  answerFormat: 2
  choices: []
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 0
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  referenceFill: '"42"'
  runTests:
  - setup: 
    expectedOutput: 42!
  explanation: Text inside quotation marks is a string. b = "42" stores the text
    42, so b + "!" joins two strings and prints 42!. Without quotes, 42 would be
    a number, and adding a number to text causes an error.
  hint: Look for the value written inside quotation marks.
  wrongChoiceFeedback: []
  wrongAnswerFeedback: Text can only be joined to text. Check that the value you
    typed is a string, which means it needs quotation marks.
